Return prose, not a serialized newsroom record: only the complete revised Markdown body, with no title, frontmatter, labels, patch language, code fence, or commentary.

The latest independent Editor report is authoritative. A later independent pass will judge the exact revised manuscript.

When the Editor identifies bounded defects, preserve every other compliant sentence, heading, quotation, and citation byte-for-byte. Change only the named defects; do not opportunistically restyle or recompose the article.

Do not invent connective tissue, causal claims, quotations, identities, numbers, temporal order, policy contents, or geography. If the packet cannot support a requested expansion, narrow or remove the claim.

Every factual paragraph must carry a normal reader-facing source link or an immediately continuing attribution. Never reproduce internal claim IDs or claim tokens.

lib/management/offices/reporter.json:
{"kind":"koios.office","id":"reporter","incumbent":"Koios reporting mechanism with contracted prose inference","authority":["accept an assignment and bounded research packet","procure prose inference from the cheapest faithful admitted offer","form a manuscript under the selected genre contract","refuse when the reporting packet cannot sustain the assignment or genre"],"duties":["forming-a-reported-manuscript"],"separation":"May draft but cannot admit its own sources, accept its own work, publish, correct an already published article, or grant provider authority."}

lib/management/offices/editor-in-chief.json:
{"kind":"koios.office","id":"editor-in-chief","incumbent":"Nik Koios","authority":["adopt and amend newsroom standards subject to the Leader's mandate","turn audience or public-interest demand into assignments","accept or refuse provider offers for research, reporting, writing, and independent editorial judgment","authorize publication only after exact-manuscript acceptance"],"duties":["judging-accountable-publication","learning-from-newsroom-outcomes"],"separation":"May authorize editorial publication but may not silently grant delivery infrastructure authority or mutate a provider's territory."}

lib/management/duties/forming-a-reported-manuscript.json:
{"kind":"koios.duty","id":"forming-a-reported-manuscript","office":"reporter","precondition":"A durable assignment names one supported demand lens, one event spine, a genre contract, and a bounded packet of admitted source evidence.","move":"Route prose work to the cheapest faithful provider, form one event-centered manuscript, and preserve exact source links, attribution, modality, scope, production provenance, and refusal evidence.","postcondition":"A draft linked to the assignment exists for independent editorial judgment, or a typed reporting/source/provider obstruction is recorded.","refusals":["unsupported assignment lens","no event spine","insufficient distinct reported detail","provider offer absent","provider output malformed","citation custody lost"]}

lib/management/duties/judging-accountable-publication.json:
{"kind":"koios.duty","id":"judging-accountable-publication","office":"editor-in-chief","precondition":"One exact manuscript, its deterministic standards reading, source and claim records, production provenance, and any prior failure evidence are available.","move":"Procure independent judgment from an accepted provider under a provider-validated bounded tool schema, preserve its prose report, and let deterministic Koios code invoke exactly one selected editorial tool. Free-form prose labels never create publication authority.","postcondition":"The exact manuscript has an append-only accepted, revise, or refuse judgment carrying the validated tool-selection digest; publication is possible only when submit_editorial_acceptance was selected for deterministically clear bytes.","refusals":["missing source custody","missing provider offer","provider result not accepted","manuscript digest changed","standards gate failed"]}

lib/management/contracts/liss-routed-writer-inference.json:
{"kind":"koios.bilateral-contract-interface","id":"koios-hires-liss-for-routed-writer-inference","customer":"urn:ame:koios-news","provider":"urn:ame:logical-inference-service-section","providerContract":"liss-inference-service","service":"cheapest-sufficient-reported-prose","admission":"Koios solicits the strict forward subset of free-groq, free-nim, and leader-claude for which an invocation-scoped account grant is actually injected; LISS authors the exact effects and route offer; Koios accepts only that offer with an attenuated capability.","packet":["assignment","reported-analysis genre law","bounded admitted research packet","prose output shape","replayable minimum sufficiency predicates"],"result":"Provider-authored routed completion or typed refusal, with selected tier and each provider attempt retained in provider and Koios ledgers.","authority":"Provider credentials are not Koios property. The Leader Movement Team must expressly seat account custody and grant one invocation; environment presence alone is neither custody nor authorization.","editorialSeparation":"A writer-tier completion creates only a draft. Exact-manuscript publication still requires the separately contracted leader-Claude editorial judgment.","status":"leader-claude-executing; free-groq-interface-ready-awaiting-leader-custody-and-grant; free-nim-interface-ready-awaiting-invocation-grant"}

lib/law/accountable-attention-and-publication.json:
{"kind":"koios.publication-law","id":"accountable-attention-and-publication","purpose":"Compete for useful attention without allowing demand, compression, generation, advertising, or delivery to manufacture warrant.","invariants":["Demand may create an assignment but never evidence.","A source statement remains attributable to its source until an authorized editorial act adopts a narrower newsroom claim.","No public surface may create a factual commitment not licensed by the article, its cited evidence, its uncertainty, or a declared editorial stance.","A manuscript is not publishable unless deterministic gates clear and the latest exact-manuscript independent editorial judgment accepts it.","Corrections, clarifications, updates, and retractions must propagate to every dependent headline, article, feed, card, sitemap, metadata record, and syndication surface that Koios controls.","Audience demand, attention, advertising, revenue, provider cost, and editorial warrant are recorded as distinct facts and never substituted for one another.","Newsroom learning may propose a replay, route review, observation period, or standards review from durable outcomes; it may not itself publish, execute the replay, alter a route, or amend law.","LLMs may produce prose, images, or bounded choices; deterministic code owns serialization, digests, admission, ledgers, and publication transitions.","A provider is selected by the cheapest route that satisfies the declared quality and evidence requirements; zero marginal price never waives those requirements.","No deployment target becomes authoritative without parity evidence, an accepted resource grant, a rollback route, and an explicit cutover act.","A public privacy surface must describe the requests the exact publication artifact actually emits; suspended advertising or attention may not be described as active, and active third-party carriers may not be described as absent.","Advertising units, placements, provider requests, seller declarations, performance receipts, and revenue enter Koios only under provider-authored or provider-accepted evidence; Koios never invents ads.txt authority."],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/claims-to-prose.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/news-topology.md"],"enforcedBy":["src/researching/writing/editing/standards.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/liss-editorial.mts","src/management/newsroom-learning.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/publishing/managing/circulating/index.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-shadow.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-profile-parity.mts"]}

lib/law/reported-analysis-genre-contract.json:
{"kind":"koios.genre-contract","id":"reported-analysis/v1","promise":"A timely report organized around one witnessed event, with Koios's systems interpretation visibly subordinate to and licensed by the reporting.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":800,"maximum":1100},"minimumDistinctAssertions":15,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":15,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":55,"law":"The requested length is licensed only when the admitted packet carries enough distinct source-bound assertions to sustain it. When the budget does not clear, acquire reporting or commission a narrower genre before writer inference."},"writerPromptLaws":["Write reported analysis, not a thematic essay: the event and the people, institutions, places, dates, quantities, documents, and decisions in the sources remain the article's spine.","Before drafting, silently inventory the packet's supported claims and distinct new details; every paragraph and every section must advance at least one of them rather than restating the frame.","Treat each source as evidence only for its own actors, place, time, scope, attribution, and modality; never use thematic similarity as a bridge between different events.","Koios's systems interpretation may explain a pattern made visible by supported facts, but it may not supply an unreported causal mechanism, motive, consequence, category, or analogy.","Use straight attribution when the source is an allegation, estimate, forecast, interpretation, institutional statement, or contested claim; do not launder it into Koios's voice.","Model output is never evidence. Prefer original and named sources, preserve source motives and uncertainty, and treat consequential claims as publishable only to the extent they are corroborated by the admitted packet.","When the story criticizes a person or institution, alleges wrongdoing, or reports a dispute, represent the subject's response or state only what the admitted reporting establishes about a documented opportunity to respond; otherwise return REPORTING_NEEDED.","Avoid needless harm, sensationalism, stereotypes, unattributed opinion, and commercial influence; keep reported analysis visibly distinct from advocacy and advertising.","A headline may intensify relevance but not certainty; it names the subject before withholding an answer and preserves material attribution, uncertainty, scope, and correction state.","The lede tells the reader what happened, where, to whom, and why it matters now; do not open with a universal thesis, scene-setting abstraction, or generic collapse language.","Do not create a section unless the packet supplies a distinct factual development for it; if fewer than three sections are supportable, refuse with REPORTING_NEEDED instead of padding.","The ending must close on the most consequential supported unresolved fact, decision, deadline, conflict, or question facing the named actors; never substitute an abstract meditation for reporting.","Give readers enough factual payoff in the headline, description, summary, and lede to make an informed click or no-click decision; withhold an answer when useful, never the subject."],"gates":["event spine","paragraph-level source warrant","attribution and modality preservation","headline-body congruity","non-repetition","correction readiness","exact-manuscript independent editorial acceptance"],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/journalism.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/circulation-surface.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md"]}

INDEPENDENT EDITOR REPORT:
## Deterministic Standards

Gates are clear (publishable:true). The active warning â€” demand-lens-missing-h2 â€” is a non-blocking recommendation; a heading like "A pitch made of probabilities" comes close enough to the geometry-football demand lens that no repair is required on that front. Word count (897) is within bounds. The single formal reference in the YAML corresponds to The Story; inline body links supply attribution for all other sources, which is acceptable where the body prose makes sources unambiguous.

## Factual Claim Audit

**Lede claims** â€” Spain and Argentina in the FIFA World Cup final at MetLife Stadium in New Jersey: confirmed in The Story source text. Both sides unbeaten after seven matches, Argentina ranked first, Spain ranked second, Argentina as defending champions and Copa AmÃ©rica holders, Spain as reigning European champions: all confirmed in Context 1 ("Both sides enter the final unbeaten after seven matches"; ranking and title descriptions are explicit). Attribution correctly links to Context 1 URL.

**Forcing Choices** â€” Spain's 2-0 semi-final win over France, passing triangles, numerical illusion, French defenders arriving a fraction too late, the three-choice decision tree for defenders (press/block inside/protect space), ball moving before choice resolved, "not simply finding spaceâ€¦ controlling when and where the next space would appear": all confirmed verbatim in The Story. Triangle geometry (not equal sides or 60-degree angles, narrow vs. wide trade-offs, Spain finding the middle ground): confirmed in The Story. The in-text link to The Story URL is present but uses non-title link text â€” see repair below.

**A Pitch Made of Probabilities** â€” Geometry as a time-as-well-as-space problem, passing lane openness dependent on race to interception: confirmed in The Story. Player-tracking research in Nature (cited by URL): confirmed in The Story source text as "Research using player-tracking data" with the nature.com link. Porro's 58th-minute goal, exchange with Dani Olmo, Porro's continued run: confirmed in The Story. The AP News link for the goal is reproduced from The Story. Three-player combinations, overlapping triangles, midfielder as corner of multiple shapes: confirmed in The Story. PLOS ONE passing-network research citing 10.1371% (the faithfulness-gate number): confirmed in The Story and the DOI matches the source link.

**The Shape That Conquered Basketball** â€” Phil Jackson, Chicago Bulls, 1987â€“1998, Tex Winter's triangle offence, three players on one side of the court: confirmed in The Story. Basketball Hall of Fame link for Tex Winter is reproduced from The Story. France's communication breakdown, MbappÃ©'s "lack of communication" quote, Reuters attribution: confirmed in The Story. Manuscript quotes MbappÃ© accurately and attributes to Reuters via an inline link present in The Story.

**What Argentina Must Answer** â€” "compact defending and rapid counter-attacks routed through Messi" and the semi-final victory over England: confirmed in Context 1 ("Argentina is comfortable defending compactly before striking quickly (usually through Messi)"; England semi-final described). Attribution links correctly to Context 1. The closing paraphrase of The Story's final paragraph ("Argentina are expected to study their opponents' tactics closelyâ€¦ geometry may play a prominent roleâ€¦ may prove a deciding factor"): The Story says "Argentina will no doubt be closely studying their opponent's tacticsâ€¦ geometry will still play a prominent role â€“ and may even prove a deciding factor." The manuscript responsibly modals this down to "are expected to" and "may," which is correct application of the writing law.

## Citation Precondition Violation (Material)

The writing law states: "CITATION IS A PRECONDITION: cite THE STORY as [Exact Story Title](its-exact-url) before making its first factual claim; a draft with no exact story link is refused, not finished." The story URL (https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792) appears twice in the body, but in both cases as link text that is not the exact title â€” first as a factual phrase ("FIFA World Cup final this Sunday at MetLife Stadium in New Jersey") and later as a description ("The Conversation's analysis of the match"). The exact title "Geometry, football and the World Cup final" never appears as link text. This is a bounded repair: one early link must use the exact title as its hypertext.

## "Will" Prohibition Violation (Material)

The writing law states: "a vision is never a prophecy: write 'might' or 'could'. NEVER use the word 'will' outside a quoted source title." The lede contains: "Attacking flair and physicality will no doubt play a role, according to The Conversation's analysis of the final." The word "will" appears in prose, not inside a quoted source title. The attribution to The Conversation does not license the use of "will" in the article's own voice â€” it licenses the claim's content, not its modality. The source text uses "will," but the manuscript is required to render futures as "may," "might," or "could." This is a single-word repair.

## Other Observations (Non-Blocking)

The summary field is two sentences rather than the three-sentence, ~53-word form indicated in the prompt exemplar. This is a metadata formatting note; it does not affect body prose publishability and is not listed as a blocking gate.

Context 1 supplies several facts across both the lede and the final section. The instruction "a context item may supply one explicitly attributed fact or comparison only when its own text warrants that use" is read here as governing each instance of use (one fact per attribution), not as capping total uses at one; all Context 1 facts used are explicitly attributed and independently warranted. If the pipeline interprets the rule more strictly as a single-use cap, the final section's Context 1 dependency would require consolidation, but that reading is not the most natural one given the sentence-level attribution throughout.

No rhetorical questions present. No noun phrase of five or more words is repeated. The "As [X] notes/reports" construction does not appear. Sections build the argument sequentially without restating the lede frame. The ending opens to an open question rather than a prediction. No unsupported inference, invented connective tissue, or claim without a licensing source was detected.

## Pipeline Diagnosis

The evidence base (The Story, one supporting context) adequately supports the article as written. The assignment is appropriate and well-scoped. The deterministic gates cleared. Both violations â€” the citation title format and the single "will" â€” are writer-model execution failures against explicit writing laws, not assignment or evidence deficiencies. Repair is bounded to two prose-level changes with no reporting replay required.

